<%# Stub KYC-provider verify page (K-440/K-443). Reached from the
    verification_url `run request_kyc` returns; the unguessable request token in
    the URL is the only credential — no sign-in. Approving signs an anonymized
    {age_over_18, licence_a} attestation for the bound agent; the documents
    themselves never leave the human. %>
<main>
  <h1>Verify your age and category-A driving licence</h1>

  <% if @request.nil? %>
    <p role="alert">
      This verification link was not recognised — it may have expired or already
      been used. Ask the assistant to start verification again.
    </p>
  <% elsif @request.status != "pending" %>
    <p>
      This verification has already been <strong><%= @request.status %></strong>.
      You can close this page.
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p>
      An assistant asked a KYC provider to confirm two facts about you so you can
      rent a combustion-engine motorcycle:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>you are over 18 (<code>age_over_18</code>), and</li>
      <li>you hold a category-A driving licence (<code>licence_a</code>).</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The provider checks your ID and licence and returns only these two
      yes/no answers, signed. Your date of birth and licence number are never
      shared with the assistant or the rental operator.
    </p>
    <form action="/kyc/verify" method="post">
      <input type="hidden" name="request" value="<%= @request.request_token %>">
      <button type="submit" name="decision" value="approve">Approve</button>
      <button type="submit" name="decision" value="decline">Decline</button>
    </form>
  <% end %>
</main>
